35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The mechanic said short runs kill the car. That explains why it feels so tired every morning.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,I saw the diary. The hours are wildly uneven. Some days are triple the load of others.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Servas,,The fuel receipts show a massive imbalance. Two of us are subsidising the rest. The tax papers show fixed costs are high.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,I found that asking for favours is what breaks groups. We need a system that removes the need to ask.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The fuel receipts and diary match. The heavy users are also the ones driving the most. The data is clear.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Servas, if short runs are the problem, we need to group trips. I can't drive a dying car.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Kenji, the uneven hours mean the current split is unfair. I want a way to balance that without arguing.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Misaki, grouping trips is wise. But we must also price the fuel correctly. The fixed costs are a separate burden.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@May, I agree. If we remove the asking, the resentment goes away. We need a schedule that feels automatic.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I agree. The fuel cost is the variable part. The tax and insurance are the fixed part. We need to separate them.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,I need the car to be clean and ready. A strict handover rule is non-negotiable for me.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"I need the coordination to be invisible. If I have to think about it, I will resent it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Servas,,"I need the math to be right. If we split fuel by usage and fixed costs equally, the subsidy disappears.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,I need the group to stay close. A system that feels like a favour is a system that will fail.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"I need the numbers to be honest. If we use the diary and receipts, we can set a fair rate per hour.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
