60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Option A is too rigid. I need the car on a Tuesday, not just my assigned day. It fails my routine.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"Option C sounds like more work. I want the coordination to disappear, not become a new chore to manage.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option C is the only one that matches cost to use. It eliminates the hidden subsidy I am worried about.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,"Option B feels like a favour. One person becomes the gatekeeper, and that is exactly what sours groups.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Option C uses the data we have. It is precise. But is it too complicated for us to keep up?,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, I agree. Option C is a chore. But Option A is a cage. I need something in between.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, I hear you. But if we don't track it, we are back to the old mess. I want the tracking to be automatic.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, it is not complicated if we use the diary we already have. The math is simple: distance times rate.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, I worry about the friction of booking. If I have to ask for a slot, it feels like a favour.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, I understand. But if the rate is fair, the asking feels less like a favour and more like a transaction.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I will vote for C. It is the only one that respects the car's condition and my need for reliability.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"I will vote for C. If the system is clear, the mental load drops. I can stop untangling debts.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,I will vote for C. It is the only option that makes the split truly even. No more hidden subsidies.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"I will vote for C. It removes the personal favour. It turns the car into a shared resource, not a gift.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I will vote for C. The data supports it. It is the most honest way to share the cost and the use.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
